# A2 Twenty Write Governance

## When to Use

Use after provider values and LLM field decisions are validated.

## Commands

```bash
python scripts/build_twenty_enrichment_write_plan.py <proposal.json> --output <plan.json>
python scripts/push_twenty_enrichment.py <plan.json> --output <dry-run.json>
python scripts/push_twenty_enrichment.py <plan.json> --apply --output <result.json>
python scripts/validate_twenty_reconciliation.py <result.json> --output <validation.json>
```

Values must originate in validated evidence. Never silently overwrite manual values, mutate one person into another, or write personal email. New People require verified identity, `CURRENT_AT_COMPANY`, and confirmed Company match. `PRIMARY` is allowed only from the primary or owner Search stage. `SECONDARY` is allowed from paid secondary Search, or from `linked_secondary` only when updating the exact verified existing Twenty Person; `linked_secondary` may never create a new Person. `a2RoleStatus` may only be `CURRENT_AT_COMPANY`, `NOT_CURRENT_AT_COMPANY`, or `UNVERIFIED`. Company email, phone and social updates use complete composite values from `build_company_contact_merge_plan.py`: preserve the existing primary, append unique website/Facebook values, verify the baseline hash immediately before PATCH, and reconcile every composite field. Generic Company channels must never populate a Person. Twenty API success is incomplete until read-back matches.